{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122436","id":4285961333,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7_dpR1","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122436","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122436.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122436.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122436","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122436/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122436/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122436/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3771d92e50833f6cb4bd7fb839ac8a3792a40f94","number":122436,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Surface orphan bits in @export_flags inspector after a flag is removed","user":{"login":"basteez","id":2451183,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTExODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2451183?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez","html_url":"https://github.com/basteez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Bugfix\r\n\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\n\r\nWhen a flag is removed from an `@export_flags` declaration, any bit that was set for the removed flag stays in the stored value. `EditorPropertyFlags` only builds checkboxes for flags that still exist, so:\r\n\r\n- `update_property()` only reflects bits that have a checkbox, so the orphaned bit never shows up in the inspector;\r\n- `_flag_toggled()` reads the full stored value and only OR/ANDs the toggled bit, so the orphaned bit survives every toggle.\r\n\r\nThe result is a bit that can't be cleared from the inspector and keeps being reported at runtime, e.g. the reproduction from the issue still printing `4` after `\"Test 3\"` is removed.\r\n\r\n### Change\r\n\r\n- Accumulate `all_flags_mask` (the OR of every value that maps to a current flag) while building the checkboxes in `setup()`.\r\n- In `update_property()`, surface every stored bit that maps to no current flag as an extra **\"Bit N (unknown flag)\"** checkbox, wired to the same `_flag_toggled()` path as regular flags. The user can untick it to clear the orphaned bit, and nothing is silently dropped.\r\n- When every named flag has been removed, the orphan checkboxes are the only controls, so the property's label/focus reference is anchored to the first one.\r\n\r\nValues with no orphaned bits are unaffected — identical UI and identical emitted values.\r\n\r\n### Alternative considered\r\n\r\nA smaller alternative is to simply mask out orphaned bits and emit the cleaned value on load. It was rejected here because it rewrites stored data on open (marking scenes/resources modified and dropping bits without the user's knowledge). Happy to switch to that approach if maintainers prefer the minimal patch.\r\n\r\n### How to verify\r\n\r\n1. Attach a script with `@export_flags(\"Test\", \"Test 2\", \"Test 3\") var test_flags = 0` and print `test_flags` in `_ready()`.\r\n2. Enable the last flag, then remove `\"Test 3\"` from the declaration.\r\n3. Before this change the removed flag's bit is invisible and still prints; with this change it appears as a **\"Bit 2 (unknown flag)\"** checkbox that can be unticked to clear it.\r\n\r\n### Known limitation (pre-existing, out of scope)\r\n\r\nPartially-set multi-bit flags declared with an explicit value (e.g. `\"Combo:6\"`) can still leave an individual bit without UI representation. This is pre-existing behavior unrelated to the positional-flag case in #72010 and would be better addressed separately.\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-15T10:57:14Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T09:11:49Z","closed_at":"2026-08-17T08:29:38Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ac94ab721705a66d908bb1a276f157f9c0ef334d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"basteez:fix-export-flags-orphan-bit-72010-show-orphans","ref":"fix-export-flags-orphan-bit-72010-show-orphans","repo":{"id":1333341679,"node_id":"R_kgDOT3kt7w","name":"godot","full_name":"basteez/godot","owner":{"login":"basteez","id":2451183,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTExODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2451183?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez","html_url":"https://github.com/basteez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basteez/subscriptions"